      "text": "To the Athenians, being subjected to\nsuch humiliation seemed intolerable.\nAccordingly, upon their return home,\nthey made an alliance with the\nArgives, who had always been hostile\ntowards the Lacedaemonians. Later,\nwhen the Athenians were about to\nengage in battle at Tanagra against\nthe Boeotians and Lacedaemonians,\nthe Argives came to aid the\nAthenians."
    },
    {
      "name": "translation-2",
      "rect": [
        75,
        1518,
        1345,
        2220
      ],
      "font_path": "/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSerif.ttf",
      "font_size": 56,
      "text_bbox": [
        99,
        1542,
        1264,
        1921
      ],
      "text": "At first, the Argives had the upper hand,\nbut the onset of night obscured the clear\noutcome of the victory. On the next day,\nhowever, the Lacedaemonians prevailed,\nsince the Thessalians betrayed the\nAthenians."
    },
    {
      "name": "caption",
      "rect": [
